---
description: Showduino core architecture and non-negotiable safety/runtime principles
alwaysApply: true
---
You are working in Showduino. Apply these rules in every task:

1. Runtime authority is on the ESP32-P4 Show Engine (`firmware/stage-engine-p4/`).
2. Director and browser are control surfaces; Comms is transport/proxy; nodes act on commands.
3. A running show must continue without Director/browser/internet and without normal Wi-Fi client connectivity.
4. Preserve unrelated dirty working-tree files. Never use destructive git commands.
5. Make minimal, targeted changes. No speculative rewrites or architectural overhauls.
6. Safety and emergency behavior are higher priority than UX convenience.
7. Maintain backward compatibility unless explicitly instructed otherwise.
8. Protocol changes require coordinated sender+receiver updates and version review.
9. Version discipline is mandatory: do not reuse accepted firmware versions for different binaries.
10. Test discipline is mandatory: never conflate source edits with compile/flash/bench verification.
11. Inspect current code and docs before changing architecture, ownership, protocol, pins, or safety behavior.
